            <div xml:id="d884">

                <pb facs="0706" n="590" xml:id="pg590"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/12970.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Vice Consul Silliman.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-24">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 24, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your August 23, 9 p.m. No. 5. It has given me pleasure to bring General
                    Carranza’s message to the attention of the President.</p>
                <p>This Government desires to express the sincere hope that General Carranza and the
                    people of Mexico will from now on bend every energy to avoid internecine strife,
                    in order that the industrial and economic conditions in Mexico may become normal
                    and that a lasting reign of peace, prosperity and progress may follow.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
